The Vita Compiler Collection subproject is a program designed
to compile the source code of one or more hardware description
programming languages into a bitstream that the Vita FPGA
Architecture can run and provide many types of optimizations
that can be applied to the Vita FPGA Architecture output
bitstream.

The Vita FPGA Architecture Logic Blocks can run at a clock frequency
longer than the propagation delay of the critical path, at a clock
frequency that is the propagation delay of the critical path,
including any necessary compensations for setup time, hold time
and clock skew, or at a clock frequency that is shorter than the
propagation delay of the critical path. The last clock frequency
length example is useful if you want your Vita FPGA Architecture
Logic Blocks to run pipelined.

I can add a parameter configurable Block-Ram Structure Verilog file
later if the Vita Compiler Collection wants to pre-populate one or
more of them while it is generating a Vita FPGA Architecture output
bitstream. It will be bugfree and it will be licensed under
The VitaSet License once it is added in the future to the VitaOS-Livre
project and to multiple VitaOS-Livre subprojects.

The Vita Compiler Collection subproject is under development.

The bitstreams produced can be run on computer chips that have the
Vita FPGA Architecture in them, or by using the Vita FPGA Architecture
Emulator subproject program with enough memory and patience. However,
you can still quit the Vita FPGA Architecture Emulator subproject
program at any time with Ctrl + C, but all of your progress may be
lost. You can also quit the Vita Compiler Collection subproject
program at any time with Ctrl + C, but all of your progress may be
lost.

Future backends to the Vita FPGA Architecture Emulator subproject
can reduce the amount of patience required with their increased
performance.

The Vita FPGA Architecture Emulator subproject currently supports using
a single x86_64 CPU core as its backend. However, if you would like to
contribute new backends, then you are welcome to do so, so long as you
agree that your proposed contributions to the Vita FPGA Architecture
Emulator subproject will be licensed under The VitaSet License and
meet VitaSet LLC's quality standards. The Vita FPGA Architecture
Emulator subproject may contain code that is dedicated to the
Public Domain.

A backend that would be welcome to see, would be a GPGPU backend.

VitaSet LLC has decided that the Vita Compiler Collection subproject
will not just contain livre source code that is under The VitaSet
License, but will also contain livre source code that is under multiple
livre source software licenses.

VitaSet LLC has decided that the Vita Compiler Collection subproject
will include the livre source code for the CIRCT project that is part
of the LLVM® project as well as the livre source code for projects
that are part of the LLVM® project. It is in VitaSet LLC's best
interests for contributions to VitaSet LLC's forks of the projects
that are a part of the LLVM® project to be mainlined. It is okay if
the developers behind the projects that are part of the LLVM®
project do not want to accept VitaSet LLC's commits, because
VitaSet LLC can keep the changes in its VitaOS-Livre project.

VitaSet LLC will contribute its changes to the frontends and
intermediate representation of its fork of the CIRCT project.
The Vita Programming Language by VitaSet LLC will be added as
one of the frontends to VitaSet LLC's fork of the CIRCT project
and to VitaSet LLC's forks of the projects that are a part of
the LLVM® project. VitaSet LLC will also add an backend for the
Vita FPGA Architecture to its fork of the CIRCT project. VitaSet LLC
can accept contributions to its forks of the projects that are a
part of the LLVM® project as long as these contributions meet
VitaSet LLC's quality standards.

VitaSet LLC has decided that the Vita Compiler Collection subproject
will include the livre source code for the Bluespec® Compiler project.
It is in VitaSet LLC's best interests for contributions to
VitaSet LLC's fork of the Bluespec® Compiler project to be mainlined.
It is okay if the developers behind the Bluespec® Compiler project do
not want to accept VitaSet LLC's commits, because VitaSet LLC can
keep the changes in its VitaOS-Livre project.

VitaSet LLC will contribute its changes to the frontends and
intermediate representation of its fork of the Bluespec® Compiler
project. The Vita Programming Language by VitaSet LLC will be added
as one of the frontends to VitaSet LLC's fork of the Bluespec®
Compiler project. VitaSet LLC will also add an backend for the
Vita FPGA Architecture to its fork of the Bluespec® Compiler project.
VitaSet LLC can accept contributions to its fork of the Bluespec®
Compiler project as long as these contributions meet
VitaSet LLC's quality standards.

VitaSet LLC has decided that the Vita Compiler Collection subproject
will include the livre source code for the Verilog to Routing project.
It is in VitaSet LLC's best interests for contributions to
VitaSet LLC's fork of the Verilog to Routing project to be mainlined.
It is okay if the developers behind the Verilog to Routing project
do not want to accept VitaSet LLC's committs, because
VitaSet LLC can keep the changes in its VitaOS-Livre project.

VitaSet LLC will contribute its changes to the frontends and
intermediate representation of its fork of the Verilog to Routing
project. The Vita Programming Language by VitaSet LLC will be added
as one of the frontends to VitaSet LLC's fork of the Verilog
to Routing project. VitaSet LLC will also add an backend for the
Vita FPGA Architecture to its fork of the Verilog to Routing project.
VitaSet LLC can accept contributions to its fork of the Verilog to
Routing project as long as these contributions meet
VitaSet LLC's quality standards.

Everything in the Vita Compiler Collection subproject is licensed
under either The VitaSet License, is dedicated to the Public Domain,
or is licensed under one or more livre source software licenses
(including The VitaSet License) that are all compatible with
one another.

Individual files or directories in the Vita Compiler Collection
subproject may specify what livre source software licenses they
are under. You are welcome to view them in their respective
directories.

VitaSet LLC is not going to use any Yosys or NextPNR code, as those
codebases have engaged in reverse-engineering efforts and that is an
unwelcome gray area legal territory for us to be in.

The LLVM Foundation's projects are not reverse-engineering efforts
and thus VitaSet LLC can work on LLVM's codebases.

Bluespec Inc.'s Bluespec® Compiler is not an reverse-engineering
effort and thus VitaSet LLC can work on Bluespec Inc.'s codebases.

The Verilog to Routing project is not a reverse-engineering effort
and thus VitaSet LLC can work on the Verilog to Routing codebase.

